# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environment
.env.local
.env

# Credentials written by the app itself — the Discord webhook URL is a bearer
# token, and this repo is public. Ignored as a directory so anything added here
# later is covered without anyone having to remember.
/.secrets/

# Data (optional - comment out if you want to commit scraped data)
# data/
# But always ignore the offer count file
data/latest_offer_count.txt

# Debug screenshots
debug_*.png

# Snapshots and console logs written by the Chrome/Playwright MCP servers when
# the app is driven through a browser by hand. Working notes, not findings.
.playwright-mcp/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Sweep results and price history under data/ ARE committed - that is how
# cloud runs get their findings back to you. A blanket `data/` rule used to
# sit here, which made the workflow's `git add data/...` a silent no-op
# (the trailing `|| true` swallowed the "paths are ignored" error), so every
# scheduled run threw its results away.
data/**/*.png
data/latest_offer_count.txt
data/20*-*-*/

# Local observations, not findings. `source_checks.json` records when each site
# was last asked for a price from *this* machine; committing it would put a
# laptop's Tuesday afternoon into a cloud sweep's history and tell you nothing.
data/source_checks.json

# A watch run's working directory - legs, searches, status - at six runs a day.
# The distilled `observations.jsonl` beside it is the finding and IS committed;
# the legs behind one observation are worth having until it is computed and not
# after, and committing them would add ~3,600 leg rows a day to the history.
data/watch/*/20*-*-*T*Z/
